I built a fast tree builder for any public GitHub repo via the linux shell.<p>`gitterbugs` (gbgs) clones, analyzes and renders a beautiful, readable and size-annotated tree of any GitHub repository in seconds.<p>For example, `gbgs <a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;torvalds&#x2F;linux">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;torvalds&#x2F;linux</a>` produces:<p>```
linux&#x2F;
├── README (4.3K)
├── Makefile (7.1K)
├── arch&#x2F;
│   └── x86&#x2F;
│       └── entry.S (1.5K)
└── init&#x2F;
    └── main.c (5.9K)
```<p>Human-readable file sizes, no junk and clean Unicode pipes for maximum legibility.
